```python
def extract(self, data):
    pose_sequence = data.get("pose_sequence", [])       # STILL frames
    walk_sequence = data.get("walk_pose_sequence", [])  # WALK frames

    # Postural entropy + tremor → use still_pose_sequence
    posture_entropy = self._calculate_posture_entropy(pose_array_still)
    tremor_scores   = self._analyze_tremor(pose_array_still)

    # Gait variability → use walk_pose_sequence (not still!)
    if walk_sequence:
        gait_var, heel_strikes = self._calculate_gait_variability(pose_array_walk)
    else:
        gait_var, heel_strikes = 0.045, np.array([])  # "Not Assessed"
```

This eliminates the core false-positive bug: sway/tremor no longer sees walking frames.

